    "title": "Environment Check-First Policy",
    "type": "pattern",
    "context": {
      "what": "Adopted a policy of checking the local environment (terminal dependencies) before suggesting any software installation.",
      "why": "To avoid redundancy, save disk space, and prevent conflict between software versions.",
      "where": "Workflow and local developer setup instructions.",
      "learned": "Always run commands like 'java -version', 'adb --version', or equivalent environment variable checks (ANDROID_HOME) before recommending a setup phase."
    },
    "tags": ["workflow", "setup", "efficiency", "best-practice"]
  },
  {
    "id": "1713506580000",
    "title": "Build Optimization and Environment Feature Toggling",
    "type": "architecture",
    "context": {
      "what": "Configured custom EAS profiles and environment-based feature visibility (conditional rendering).",
      "why": "To speed up builds via local execution and hide developer tools from end users.",
      "where": "eas.json, ProfileMenu.tsx, ProfileScreen.tsx",
      "learned": "Using EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix for environment variables ensures they are baked into the build at compile time, allowing for reliable UI variant switching."
    },
